reply:
An emergency, such as a burst pipe, is subject to the after-hours hourly rate if it occurs between 6:00 PM and 8:00 AM on weekdays or all day on weekends and public holidays. The after-hours hourly rate is 1.5 times the standard rate of $165 per hour. Additionally, an emergency dispatch fee of $149 applies. For non-emergency leak repairs on exposed pipes, the price starts from $175, while hidden or in-wall leaks are quoted on site.
